From 2aa64ef15e709b6d7ecaf15f3ca678c28456ce7a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:13:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban chat links: release a compressed chat's
 owner-written ancestor row; owner skips cron_ chats; task_id index

Follow-up to PR #2095 (review comment 5889574415, three non-blocking findings).

1. Compressed chat during the outage. The owner publishes a chat's link from the card's `platform='hub'`
   subscription, which names the session that placed the card (S0). A chat that compressed before its gateway's
   accept_binding (Board sync down) has its ledger resolve the tip S1, so the card had two unreleased rows: S0 from
   the owner, S1 from the chat gateway. session_tasks deduped them, but links_diff listed S0 only_in_replica until
   the card closed. The chat gateway's reconcile now releases an owner-written row on an open card whose chat
   session is a compression ancestor of a session it already links, unreleased, to the same card and chat profile
   (`_compressed_away`, walking `_CHAIN_STEP_SQL` in that profile's state.db; an unreadable state.db releases
   nothing). The owner never writes S0 back: a released row is still a row (insert-only rule from #2095).
2. cron_ sessions. `_owner_hub_links` filtered only headless worker hashes; it now uses `machine_sessions`, the
   verdict the chat gateway releases by, so a `cron_` chat's sub no longer gets a row that gateway would release on
   its next pass. A foreign ref is never looked up locally, so no state.db read is added.
3. Index. `task_chat_links(task_id)` index in SYNC_SCHEMA_SQL (board files, link-only files and replicas all run it
   through `install_or_remove`; IF NOT EXISTS on first open is the migration). An index is no column, so it does not
   touch `SchemaAhead`/wire versioning. On worker-4's replica copy (17k links) the owner's 265-id IN lookup went from
   2.81 ms (SCAN) to 0.38 ms (SEARCH USING INDEX); the other task_chat_links plans are unchanged except the
   released-sibling EXISTS of `_read_replica_links`, which now searches by task_id.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_chat_links_owner_hub_subs.py), each failing on main:
- test_a_chat_compressed_during_the_outage_keeps_one_unreleased_row_and_a_clean_diff: two gateways on the fake Board,
  sync given up the real way, chat compresses S0->S1 before recovery; after reconcile exactly one unreleased row (S1),
  S0 released, links_diff clean, the owner adds nothing.
- test_owner_skips_a_cron_session_the_chat_gateway_would_release.
- test_task_chat_links_has_a_task_id_index_in_board_files_and_replicas_and_migrates_old_files (query plan, migration
  of a file without the index, schema_ahead still empty).
Guard: test_an_uncompressed_second_chat_on_the_same_card_keeps_its_owner_row (passes before and after).
168 related test files (chat links, sync, schema guard, board delivery): 3712 passed, 1 failed (a bulk-provenance
fixture passing `want` entries without keys; `_compressed_away` now reads them with .get), that file then green.

Card: t_01a1d480e6d8fd12
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_chat_links.py               |  68 ++++++++++-
 hermes_cli/kanban_db_sync.py                  |   5 +
 .../test_kanban_chat_links_owner_hub_subs.py  | 114 ++++++++++++++++++
